## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of attention math, dimensions, scaling, and how tokenization affects token-to-token alignment in real models.

## Key Concepts

- Dot-product attention math and scaling (√d_k)
- Softmax over keys for each query
- Tokenization impact on alignment
- Practical pitfalls in batching

## Code Example

```javascript
function simpleAttention(q, k, v) {
  // q: [d], k: [n, d], v: [n, d]
  const scores = k.map(row => dot(q, row) / Math.sqrt(d));
  const weights = softmax(scores);
  return weights.reduce((acc, w, idx) => acc + w * v[idx], 0);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical RAG design for payments, emphasizing chunking, embedding sizing, vector DB indexing, latency, and freshness controls in real-world contexts.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
- Document chunking and overlap strategies
- Vector databases (e.g., Pinecone, Weaviate)
- Re-ranking and freshness management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: chunk 4KB with 25% overlap
const CHUNK_SIZE = 4 * 1024;
const OVERLAP = Math.floor(CHUNK_SIZE * 0.25);
function chunk(doc) {
  const blocks = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < doc.length; i += CHUNK_SIZE - OVERLAP) {
    blocks.push(doc.slice(i, i + CHUNK_SIZE));
  }
  return blocks;
}
```

